# A spawned concurrent task (fiber). The clean uniform interface; each backend runs the work on its concurrency runtime (node event-loop promise, rust tokio task, swift Task, kotlin coroutine) behind this API. The running task lives in the opaque `dock` handle. spawn starts the work and returns immediately; wait awaits its completion.

load @cluesurf/base/code/native/fiber
  find do-spawn
  find do-wait

# a running concurrent task
form fiber
  link dock, like fiber-handle

  # wait for the fiber to finish
  task wait
    note async
    take self
    like void
    call do-wait
      read self
      wait true

# run `work` concurrently, returning a fiber to wait on
task spawn
  take work
    like task
      like void
  like fiber
  send back
    make fiber
      bind dock
        call do-spawn
          read work
